attorneys.bio:
Eric Lubin, Esq. is the chair of Lomurro Law's commercial and general litigation department. Eric enjoys a wealth of courtroom experience, having tried multiple jury and bench trials in several different fields of law, such as: corporate; trust & estates; personal injury; contract; employment; and criminal. Eric also regularly advises and represents businesses and professionals in matters involving partner/member disputes, contracts, employment controversies and regulatory violations.

A large concentration of Eric's practice also includes transactional work for businesses. Eric's scope of representation ranges from helping clients start businesses to representing international companies through multimillion-dollar transactions. In this regard, Eric commonly consults with tax professionals and other experts in their fields. Eric also provides in-house legal services to several companies. Eric also represents non-profits and sits on their boards and committees to improve the quality of Monmouth County.

Some of Eric's notable achievements include

Obtaining appeal victory that reversed a trial court and then procuring a $3,400,000.00 verdict in a fiduciary abuse case based upon improper hedge fund investments by a trustee;

o Successful negotiation and sale of a $65,000,000.00 promissory note and related debt instrument in a decades-long commercial dispute;

o Dismissal of all claims made against a client, an international law firm, in defamation related case;

o Six-figure jury verdict on behalf of corporate client in case alleging corporate espionage based on the New Jersey Trade Secrets Act;

o Published appellate victory requiring National Bank to provide indemnification to corporate agent under New Jersey Business Corporation Act;

o Providing advice and negotiation for adversarial buyout of a partner for a well-known restaurant brand;

o Obtaining dismissal of multimillion-dollar claims made by gamblers in a defective casino game under the New Jersey Casino Control Act and then negotiation of recoupment of all losses with insurance company; and

o Six-figure verdict on behalf of client and dismissal of all counterclaims in a dispute between former law partners regarding the breakup of their practice.

Ensuring that the goals of a client's representation are met in a timely, effective and cost-efficient manner is of the utmost importance to Eric. In this regard, Eric's prior clients have given the following testimonials:

"Mr. Lubin assisted me with contract review, editing, and insight in the most professional and precise manner. He found all the areas of interest in a lengthy contract and made a potentially stressful business transition a breeze. He was also very reasonable with billing and advised me of the most win-win approach to getting my contracts finalized. Thank you! I will be reaching out soon for assistance with future projects!"

" I cannot stress enough at how efficient, knowledgeable, and hardworking Eric is. Was always available for contact through a trying situation. Thank you for all your hard work. Would recommend Eric to anyone!"

"I have retained Eric several times over the past few years. Sometimes I have not been happy with his advice and wanted to do things my own way. But, as things progress, I have seen that his advice had been correct and it's always appreciated. My company and I have been better off with Eric as our litigation counsel."

"Eric did a great job for us during a business dispute. He was the third attorney picking up from where we had left off with previous counsel. He was able to put us into a position of strength, which was where we should have been operating from. This allowed us to turn the tables on the partner who had gone rogue. It turned out about as good as it could have in the situation we were in. His assistance was critical in achieving this outcome."

Awards and Honors

Honors

Rising Star, Super Lawyers Magazine, 2012-2013

